                                "sense_id": "d4de9776-ccb5-3dc5-bc75-422ae089d884",
                                "text": "If pressure continues, the area remains erythemic and will not blanch. Eventually, the skin may appear pale due to the extended ischemia."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c27a777-e45a-4a1b-b149-b4a647be8b0c",
                                "sense_id": "d4de9776-ccb5-3dc5-bc75-422ae089d884",
                                "text": "Scores were totaled for treatment groups of 4-8 pigs at each grading period and the percent of maximum erythemic response determined or the average erythemic score was determined."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02da6cac-7853-4df6-987e-f675ee003826",
                                "sense_id": "d4de9776-ccb5-3dc5-bc75-422ae089d884",
                                "text": "Skin may be erythemic, lacerated, or bleeding, and encrustations may be seen on the skin, stoma, or old appliance (white sandpaper-textured particles)."
                            },
